                                <h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-white mb-2">1. Initial Vessel Processing</h3>
                                <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed border-l-4 border-pink-500 pl-4">
                                    The raw sample vessel geometry is loaded into the pipeline, where the input and output boundaries are automatically detected and capped. This topology-preservation step is crucial for defining valid boundary conditions for subsequent fluid simulations.
                                </p>
                            </div>
                        </div>

                        <!-- 2. Centerlines -->
                        <div class="bg-gray-800 rounded-lg overflow-hidden border border-gray-700 shadow-xl">
                            <img src="images/medical-simulation/vessel-centerlines.png" alt="Vessel Centerlines" class="w-full h-auto object-cover opacity-90 hover:opacity-100 transition-opacity duration-300">
                            <div class="p-6">
                                <h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-white mb-2">2. Centerline Computation</h3>
                                <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed border-l-4 border-pink-500 pl-4">
                                    Vascular centerlines are computationally calculated using wave-propagation from a user-defined seed point. The <span class="text-blue-400 font-bold">blue line</span> explicitly identifies the aneurysm sac, distinguishing it from the main arterial flow path.
                                </p>
                            </div>
                        </div>

                        <!-- 3. Parent Vessel Extraction -->
                        <div class="bg-gray-800 rounded-lg overflow-hidden border border-gray-700 shadow-xl">
                            <img src="images/medical-simulation/parent-vessel-extraction.png" alt="Parent Vessel Extraction" class="w-full h-auto object-cover opacity-90 hover:opacity-100 transition-opacity duration-300">
                            <div class="p-6">
                                <h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-white mb-2">3. Parent Vessel Extraction</h3>
                                <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed border-l-4 border-pink-500 pl-4">
                                   The parent vessel geometry is mathematically isolated by tracing along the computed centerline. This effectively separates the healthy artery from the pathology, defining the precise "landing zone" required for the flow diverter.
                                </p>
                            </div>
                        </div>

                        <!-- 4. Mock Stent -->
                        <div class="bg-gray-800 rounded-lg overflow-hidden border border-gray-700 shadow-xl">
                            <img src="images/medical-simulation/mock-stent.png" alt="Mock Stent" class="w-full h-auto object-cover opacity-90 hover:opacity-100 transition-opacity duration-300">
